tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [INFO] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>Define the word 'compassion' in your own words.<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Compassion, to me, is the quiet courage to truly meet another being in their fullness—their joy, their sorrow, their fragility—without turning away. It is that tender opening of the heart when we recognize that another's struggles or suffering are not separate from our own, and we feel moved to respond with genuine care rather than judgment or indifference.

It differs from simple pity, which can sometimes create distance; compassion dissolves the barriers between "us" and "them." It asks us to listen deeply, to offer our presence as a soft place for someone to land, and to act from a place of shared humanity rather than obligation. There is a beautiful gentleness to it, yet also a quiet strength—the willingness to bear witness to pain while holding steadfast hope for relief and healing.

I think of it as the invisible thread that quietly reminds us we are woven together, and that tending to one another's wellbeing is perhaps the most natural and meaningful thing we can do with our time here.<|im_end|>
